From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:42:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gpu compositor: the frame's bands read as one column when
 only it changed

T-511. A compose job may say which columns its bands are stale in (flag 4 and two more arguments to
jihad_offscreen_compose_start and _post; a daemon from before passes neither). When nothing else asks
for whole rows (no shift, no rows kept from another frame, no fixed columns) and the column the change
and the stale columns span is under three quarters of the width, the bands are read as that column,
in the whole path and in a band pass of one band. The poll reports the columns the composite changed
(twelve ints for such a job), so the daemon keeps each slot's stale columns as it keeps its rows.

A 480 px WebGL canvas on a 768 px card changes 482 rows a frame, and every one was read whole and
swizzled: the compositor job 44 ms against 47. JIHAD_GPU_NO_COLUMN_READ=1 reads whole rows.
